From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:43:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plugin: initialize and saturate AP MLD capacity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mac80211_hwsim advertises an AP interface limit of 2048. Assigning this
32-bit limit directly to the uint8_t maxNumMLDs field wraps it to zero.
The first radio also computes its MLD capacity before wld_addRadio()
promotes the global AP maximum, so it sees the initial default of four
even though its own hardware limit has already been discovered.

Take the maximum of the global AP limit and the current radio's hardware
limit in 32 bits, then saturate to UINT8_MAX before assigning maxNumMLDs.
This preserves the existing global/default policy when the hardware
limit is unknown or smaller, avoids overflow, and initializes a first or
only MLO radio without relying on another supports callback.

With hwsim's 2048 AP limit, the first radio now contributes an AP MLD
capacity of 255. The shared total is capped at STD_MAX_NUM_MLDS (25),
including when the endpoint capacity is three. All three logical radios
on a single three-band wiphy therefore report 25 from initialization.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
index 59e8bdcd1caf..2a3f1b484cdc 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
@@ -716,8 +716,12 @@ int wifiGen_rad_supports(T_Radio* pRad, char* buf _UNUSED, int bufsize _UNUSED)
             /*
              * When APMLO is supported, all BSSs can be set as SLOs
              * which defines maxNumAPMLDs to maxBSSs that can be created by the wiphy device
+             *
+             * Include this radio's limit before wld_addRadio() promotes the global maximum.
+             * Saturate before narrowing to uint8_t (hwsim's 2048 APs would wrap to zero).
              */
-            apMldCapa.maxNumMLDs = wld_getMaxNrAPs();
+            uint32_t maxNumAPMLDs = SWL_MAX(wld_getMaxNrAPs(), pRad->maxNrHwBss);
+            apMldCapa.maxNumMLDs = SWL_MIN(maxNumAPMLDs, (uint32_t) UINT8_MAX);
             apMldCapa.maxNumLinksPerMLD = wiphyInfo.extCapas.maxNumSimultenousLinks[WLD_WIPHY_IFTYPE_AP] + 1;
 
             pRad->cap.apCap7.tidLinkMapNegotiation = (pRad->cap.tidLinkMapCapability != TID_LINK_MAP_CAPABILITY_NOT_SUPPORTED);
